1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,220
Reactions, with heat on the arrow.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:05,700
Complex ions and their charges.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,540
Match-the-list tables.

4
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:10,340
Structures, right inside the question.

5
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,420
This is chemistry in TestoZa

6
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,846
and in the next few minutes, you'll type all of it yourself.

7
00:00:17,896 --> 00:00:20,936
We'll use real questions from JEE Main and JEE Advanced

8
00:00:20,936 --> 00:00:22,056
2026.

9
00:00:22,056 --> 00:00:25,736
Open Create Test, give it a name, pick JEE marking…

10
00:00:25,736 --> 00:00:27,442
and straight to the questions.

11
00:00:27,612 --> 00:00:31,612
First, a JEE Main question on complex ions.

12
00:00:31,612 --> 00:00:33,372
The words, you just type.

13
00:00:33,372 --> 00:00:36,332
For the formulas, open Maths and symbols

14
00:00:36,332 --> 00:00:37,932
this is Sy Pad

15
00:00:37,932 --> 00:00:39,646
and go to the Chemistry tab.

16
00:00:39,816 --> 00:00:44,136
Now, the most useful button for any chemistry teacher

17
00:00:44,136 --> 00:00:45,096
Formula.

18
00:00:45,096 --> 00:00:47,576
Just type the formula the way you'd write it.

19
00:00:47,576 --> 00:00:50,136
Bracket, M n, B r, four…

20
00:00:50,136 --> 00:00:50,856
see?

21
00:00:50,856 --> 00:00:53,496
The four drops down on its own.

22
00:00:53,496 --> 00:00:57,276
For the charge, type a caret, then two minus.

23
00:00:57,446 --> 00:00:59,046
Then the copper complex

24
00:00:59,046 --> 00:01:01,046
six waters, two plus.

25
00:01:01,046 --> 00:01:05,606
Insert, and Formula again for the two nickel complexes.

26
00:01:05,606 --> 00:01:09,446
Every number drops down and every charge goes up,

27
00:01:09,446 --> 00:01:10,806
while you type.

28
00:01:10,806 --> 00:01:11,606
Insert…

29
00:01:11,606 --> 00:01:14,486
and the whole line sits right in the question.

30
00:01:14,486 --> 00:01:17,941
The options are plain text, and D is the right answer.

31
00:01:18,111 --> 00:01:19,951
Next, an equilibrium.

32
00:01:19,951 --> 00:01:22,911
Type the first line, then Formula, A,

33
00:01:22,911 --> 00:01:25,951
the gas key, the reversible arrow, B…

34
00:01:25,951 --> 00:01:27,231
and gas again.

35
00:01:27,401 --> 00:01:30,361
The other keys work the same way: gas given off,

36
00:01:30,361 --> 00:01:33,241
a precipitate, heat, degree Celsius,

37
00:01:33,241 --> 00:01:38,201
aqueous, solid, liquid, K a, K b, pH and mol.

38
00:01:38,201 --> 00:01:39,162
One tap each.

39
00:01:39,659 --> 00:01:40,699
Insert.

40
00:01:40,699 --> 00:01:42,459
Now the rest of the question

41
00:01:42,459 --> 00:01:45,419
the concentrations, and what happens when we add more

42
00:01:45,419 --> 00:01:46,219
A.

43
00:01:46,219 --> 00:01:48,831
Then the four options, and D again.

44
00:01:49,826 --> 00:01:53,186
Now, three reactions with conditions on the arrows.

45
00:01:53,186 --> 00:01:56,146
Formula, sodium tetraborate…

46
00:01:56,146 --> 00:01:59,666
then the arrow with a box above and below.

47
00:01:59,666 --> 00:02:02,946
Here you choose how many lines go above and below.

48
00:02:02,946 --> 00:02:06,706
We only need one, on top, so remove the bottom one,

49
00:02:06,706 --> 00:02:07,858
and Insert.

50
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:10,988
That question mark above the arrow is your blank.

51
00:02:10,988 --> 00:02:14,748
Tap delta for heat, step past the arrow with this key,

52
00:02:14,748 --> 00:02:16,188
and finish the reaction.

53
00:02:16,188 --> 00:02:16,973
Insert.

54
00:02:17,663 --> 00:02:20,863
Second reaction: copper sulphate plus Y.

55
00:02:20,863 --> 00:02:21,903
Same arrow

56
00:02:21,903 --> 00:02:26,463
but now tap Words, and type non-luminous flame.

57
00:02:26,463 --> 00:02:29,183
Words keep their spaces, like normal text.

58
00:02:29,183 --> 00:02:29,930
Insert.

59
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:34,350
And the third one: two Z, two X and carbon on the left,

60
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:36,830
the arrow with luminous flame on top,

61
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:40,750
and two Q, borax and carbon monoxide on the right

62
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,590
exactly the same way.

63
00:02:42,590 --> 00:02:43,710
Insert.

64
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:46,190
Type the question, the four options

65
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:48,190
plus two and plus two, and so on

66
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:49,531
and B is correct.

67
00:02:51,677 --> 00:02:52,557
Match the list

68
00:02:52,557 --> 00:02:53,997
JEE Main loves these.

69
00:02:53,997 --> 00:02:57,517
In Sy Pad, open Tables, and choose Match List.

70
00:02:57,517 --> 00:03:00,157
List-I and List-II are already there.

71
00:03:00,157 --> 00:03:01,117
Type the labels

72
00:03:01,117 --> 00:03:03,357
A, B, C, D and one to four

73
00:03:03,357 --> 00:03:04,132
and Insert.

74
00:03:04,302 --> 00:03:06,542
Every empty cell is now a blue box.

75
00:03:06,542 --> 00:03:10,542
Click one, tap Formula, and type XeO3.

76
00:03:10,542 --> 00:03:12,462
Next box

77
00:03:12,462 --> 00:03:12,942
XeF2…

78
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:17,182
and so on, down both lists: XeO2F2,

79
00:03:17,182 --> 00:03:21,582
XeOF4, then BrF5, NH3, the I3 minus ion,

80
00:03:21,582 --> 00:03:22,576
and SF4.

81
00:03:24,853 --> 00:03:25,653
Insert

82
00:03:25,653 --> 00:03:28,773
and there it is: a clean two-column table,

83
00:03:28,773 --> 00:03:31,573
right inside the question, just like the paper.

84
00:03:31,573 --> 00:03:33,093
Type the four options

85
00:03:33,093 --> 00:03:35,493
A two, B one, and so on

86
00:03:35,493 --> 00:03:36,969
and B is the answer.

87
00:03:37,959 --> 00:03:40,919
Now JEE Advanced, Paper 1.

88
00:03:40,919 --> 00:03:44,039
The answer here is a number, so change the question type

89
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,479
to Numerical answer.

90
00:03:45,479 --> 00:03:49,079
And JEE Advanced takes nothing off for a wrong number,

91
00:03:49,079 --> 00:03:50,999
so set Wrong to zero.

92
00:03:50,999 --> 00:03:53,239
You can set the marks on any question,

93
00:03:53,239 --> 00:03:54,092
like this.

94
00:03:54,262 --> 00:03:55,462
Type the question.

95
00:03:55,462 --> 00:03:56,902
Now the first structure

96
00:03:56,902 --> 00:03:59,782
tap Picture, then this cloud button.

97
00:03:59,782 --> 00:04:02,742
It puts a picture inside the text, exactly where your

98
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:03,702
cursor is.

99
00:04:03,702 --> 00:04:07,062
Choose a picture, find your file, pick the structure…

100
00:04:07,062 --> 00:04:08,086
and there it is.

101
00:04:08,256 --> 00:04:11,776
Now open Sy Pad, and right next to the structure,

102
00:04:11,776 --> 00:04:13,776
the arrow with conditions.

103
00:04:13,776 --> 00:04:18,176
Tap Words, type heat on top, add X,

104
00:04:18,176 --> 00:04:19,696
and Insert.

105
00:04:19,696 --> 00:04:23,216
The second structure goes in exactly the same way:

106
00:04:23,216 --> 00:04:27,056
Picture, the cloud button, choose the file.

107
00:04:27,056 --> 00:04:28,976
Then Sy Pad again

108
00:04:28,976 --> 00:04:33,056
the arrow, the word heat on top, and Y.

109
00:04:33,056 --> 00:04:33,927
Insert.

110
00:04:35,028 --> 00:04:36,308
Just like the paper.

111
00:04:36,308 --> 00:04:38,788
For the answer, choose Exact value,

112
00:04:38,788 --> 00:04:39,953
and type four.

113
00:04:40,896 --> 00:04:42,496
And when a question is long

114
00:04:42,496 --> 00:04:44,256
don't type it at all.

115
00:04:44,256 --> 00:04:46,336
More than one answer can be right here,

116
00:04:46,336 --> 00:04:48,496
so first choose Multiple correct.

117
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:51,616
Now Fill from photo, choose a photo of the question…

118
00:04:51,616 --> 00:04:53,480
and TestoZa reads it for you.

119
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:56,530
All three reactions, the gas labels,

120
00:04:56,530 --> 00:05:00,450
the 573 kelvin, even U-235

121
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:03,570
and the photo shows the answer, so A and C are already

122
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:04,260
ticked.

123
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:06,510
Always give it one quick read.

124
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:07,470
Last thing

125
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:08,670
partial marks.

126
00:05:08,670 --> 00:05:12,510
Choose JEE Advanced: one mark for each correct option

127
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:15,293
picked, full marks only for all of them.

128
00:05:18,879 --> 00:05:20,159
Save test…

129
00:05:20,159 --> 00:05:23,039
and your chemistry paper is in My Tests

130
00:05:23,039 --> 00:05:25,198
ready to conduct as a live exam.

131
00:05:26,442 --> 00:05:29,482
Formulas, reactions, tables and structures

132
00:05:29,482 --> 00:05:30,762
all in one place.

133
00:05:30,762 --> 00:05:33,642
Make your chemistry test at testoza.com.

134
00:05:33,642 --> 00:05:36,304
Subscribe for more, and I'll see you in the next one.
